  "articleBody": "Finish carpentry might look simple, but there are several common pitfalls that can really diminish the quality of the final product. Knowing what to watch out for can save you a lot of grief and ensure a beautiful result. Firstly, poor measurements are a huge no-no; inaccurate cuts lead to unsightly gaps and wasted material, so precise measuring is paramount. Another mistake is using mismatched profiles or wood species; consistency is key to a cohesive look. Visible gaps at corners or along joints can scream 'amateur job,' so tight, clean fits are essential. Nail pops, where nails aren't set properly or the wood shifts, are also a common issue, requiring careful fastening techniques. Over-caulking, where too much caulk is used to hide gaps, often looks messy and draws attention to imperfections rather than concealing them. Lastly, installing trim before walls are fully dry or stable can lead to movement and cracking down the line. A professional like HH Remodeling LLC avoids these common errors, ensuring your finish carpentry is done right the first time.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}